Steps to correct code:
Review all variable declarations for spelling and correct data types
Check that every input statement has a matching variable
Trace the program one line at a time using sample data
Verify calculations are performed correctly
Check loop conditions to ensure they terminate properly
Test both passing and failing scenarios to verify the program produces the expected output





start
   Declarations
      num firstTest
      num secondTest
      num average
      num PASSING = 60

   output "Enter first score or 0 to quit"
   input firstTest

   while firstTest <> 0
      output "Enter second score"
      input secondTest

      average = (firstTest + secondTest) / 2

      output "Average is ", average

      if average >= PASSING then
         output "Pass"
      else
         output "Fail"
      endif

      output "Enter first score or 0 to quit"
      input firstTest
   endwhile
stop
